    <string name="CC_SCOPE_DETAIL">All %1$s games share one mapping. This game only: a copy for this game alone, changed without touching the others; back to all games drops it.</string>
    <string name="CC_LEAD">What the %1$s game gets from your pad. Left and right change the button, Y puts the usual ones back. The launcher and the game\'s menu keep the usual buttons; the on-screen pad is never remapped.</string>
    <string name="CC_RANGE">Stick range</string>
    <string name="CC_RANGE_DETAIL">How far the game\'s stick goes at your stick\'s full travel; a real N64 stick reaches about 80. Usual: 80.</string>
    <string name="CC_DEADZONE">Dead zone</string>
    <string name="CC_DEADZONE_DETAIL" formatted="false">How far your stick moves before the game sees it. Raise it if a character walks on its own. Usual: 8 %.</string>
    <string name="CC_RUNTIME_DEFAULT">Usual</string>
    <string name="CC_RESET_DETAIL">Every %1$s button back to its usual place (for %2$s).</string>
    <string name="CC_TOUCH_DETAIL">The %1$s\'s own buttons on the game\'s screen, never remapped. Without a controller: shown while no controller is connected, hidden as soon as one is used. The in-game menu shows or hides it for the session. Never on a handheld\'s top screen while the bottom screen shows the panel.</string>
